arf, classic frequency counter ^^

```javascript
function countChars(str) {
  let result = {};
  for (let i = 0; i < str.length; i++){
    let char = str[i];
    if (result[char]) {
      result[char]++;
    } else {
      result[char] = 1;
    }
  }
  return result;
}
```

use it like this:

```javascript
let string = "hello, world.";
let charCount = countChars(string);
console.log(charCount); // returns { ' ': 1, ',': 1, '.': 1, e: 1, h: 1, l: 3, o: 2, r: 1, w: 1 }
```

it walks the string one character at a time -- if that character's already a key, bump the count, otherwise start it at 1. by the end you've got a full tally of every character in the string, wan~

